        "rationale": "Within the non-empty Python str input scope, guess_filename reads obj.name and returns os.path.basename(name) only when name[0] != '<' and name[-1] != '>'. A name starting with '<' OR ending with '>' fails the guard and yields implicit None. The scope excludes bytes: byte indexing yields integers, so the existing character comparisons do not establish the same placeholder filtering for bytes.",
